# bay time 358.3 s
# A move of an arm from one pose to the next: 1.5 x the largest over its six joints of |change| / (the datasheet's greatest speed of that joint), the factor for speeding up and slowing down; its carriage moves at the same time and takes distance / speed + speed / acceleration of the track; the longer of the two counts, then 0.3 s to settle. A move with no change takes nothing. Moves go straight from the pose at one point to the pose at the next: the approaches and retreats are checked by the approach rows but not timed, and the paths between are not modelled or checked.
# A working step is its move from the arm's last pose and the layout's process time for the kind. A tool change takes the arm's tool_change_s; the move to where the tools wait is not counted. Every arm starts the bay at its wait pose with its first tool, and each step is done by the arm the layout's division of the kind's points gives it.
# The bay: tube in + clamp + the rail phase + the module phase + the end. A phase is a row of units (the ten rails; the nine modules). Each unit has a leading piece, its take and its set, by the arms that have them, and following pieces: a rail's strap bolt; a module's locating, pinning and swaging of its four holes, an arm's pin magazine counted with the module before whose holes it takes it. Each arm does its pieces in the order of the steps (the layout's rail_order for the rails); a following piece on unit k starts when every leading piece of unit k has ended and its arm has ended its pieces before it; a set of unit k starts when every leading piece of unit k-1 has ended (the rails and the modules go on in order); and the phase ends when the last arm ends. With one leading and one following arm this is the following arm one unit behind: the largest over k of (the leading arm's pieces on units 0..k + the following arm's on units k..end); when one arm does the whole phase, the plain sum. An arm's pieces include its tool changes. The time has no limit: its row passes when every step has a pose. The end: release + bay out, or the longest of the arms' moves back to their wait poses and first tools if that is longer.
# margins: clearance 0.015 m, joint margin 5.0 deg
# posture module_arm: largest change 2.15 s between module_set 8 and wait; 1 changes above 2.0 s
# posture pin_arm_a: largest change 1.30 s between tool change and pins_take 0; 0 changes above 2.0 s
# posture pin_arm_c: largest change 0.87 s between strap_bolt 7 and strap_bolt 8; 0 changes above 2.0 s
# posture pin_arm_b: largest change 1.53 s between swage 5/0 and wait; 0 changes above 2.0 s
